two years touring the continent, and ended up drawing a map of a plausible
redivision of the U.S., Canada, and Mexico in terms of similarity of
climate and resources, ethnic background, geography, etc.  Even if you
don't agree with all of Garreau's conclusions, it makes a fascinating read
and an excellent travelogue (circa 1983 or so).

