she has what could be an optical illusion to bolster her case.  I'm not
aware of anything to support the claim that she's an agent provacateur.  It
seems far more likely to me that she's just the sort of person who's so
locked into the right-wing mindset that she leaps to violent tactical
proposals without adequate justification.  She's far from the only one who
suffers from this.  I know another guy who thinks "we" can win a short
violent conflict with the Feds if we plan our sabotage right.

James Daugherty got it right: the battle of ideas is where it's at right
now and for the forseeable future.  While it makes just as much sense to
be prepared for domestic tyranny as it does for natural disasters, we need
to focus on ideological conflict.

